From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:50:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] ci: build and test patched backend images on hosted
 runners

Build the optimized amd64 backend on a bounded Ubuntu runner. Reuse build
layers through a registry cache and persist the compiler cache across runs.
Share source and dependency layers between runtime and test targets so a
test-only dispatch can skip the release build.

Check runtime tools and SQLite startup before publication. Publish the
source tag and immutable image digest together so the source stays
reachable across rebases. Run deployment receipt and Node action-tree
regressions after publication, or run them alone with publish_image=false.
